Axios is used in the application code to make API calls, so it is required when the app runs in production.

@types/node is only used during development to provide TypeScript type support. It is not needed when the app is running, so it does not get included in production.

“I use Prettier for formatting and ESLint for code quality. I configure scripts like format and lint --fix so issues can be automatically corrected across the project.”

Prettier → formatting (spaces, semicolons)
ESLint → logic issues (unused vars, bad patterns)
Both together → clean + consistent codebase


